fixture tech09_reverse_pogo
doc BUILD.md s5 tech 9 "Reverse pogo: pogo while moving backward to reposition behind an enemy. Taught by a shielded enemy"; s5 Pogo "Horizontal speed fully preserved". Ash dashes at an enemy-sized block (the shield faces Ash), short-hops on a dash-jump, turns back to face the block and strikes down at it while still flying forward: the bounce keeps the forward speed, so Ash sails over and lands behind the block facing its back
room test/shield
spawn 350 544
frames 80
input
  0 R dash
  1..5 R
  # A short hop on dash frame 7: a dash-jump, so the dash's speed carries on.
  6..7 R jump
  8..11 R
  # Back and down with the strike: Ash turns to face the block while the jump still carries
  # forward. Any strike on ticks 9 to 14 bounces off the block and lands behind it.
  12 L D attack
  13..79
end
expect
  at 6 event.jump=1 vx=5120
  at 12 facing=-1 vx>0
  # The down-strike's box finds the block's head: moving forward, facing back.
  mark bounce 13..20 event.pogo=1
  at bounce facing=-1 vx>2304
  # Over the block and down behind it, its body clear of the block's back (672 u), still facing it.
  mark land bounce+1..79 event.land=1
  at land x>682u y=544u facing=-1
  during bounce..land facing=-1
end
